// Rank agreement between the triage formula and a dispatcher's working order.
//
// Each case is a WHOLE QUEUE with an ordering attached, because a ranking is a property of
// a set - scoring incidents one at a time would measure something nobody uses. The label is
// whether rank correlation clears the 0.85 target from the proposal.
//
// The dispatcher orderings here are **agreed expectations, not recorded shifts.** No
// labelled corpus of real dispatcher decisions exists yet; these are written from the
// weights' own stated intent - immediate danger first, then scale, then how long somebody
// has waited - so this is a regression gate on the formula rather than a measure of
// agreement with a human. When file 28 lands a real corpus, these are replaced and the
// number starts meaning what its name says.
